course: dictionary
lesson: 4046
title: Gender and grammar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word gender has two main meanings. The first is about people: being a boy or a girl, a man or a woman, and the roles and ideas that societies link with each one. Some people feel they are both, neither, or not the gender they were thought to be at birth, and everyone deserves kindness and respect about this.
explain: The second meaning is about grammar. In languages like French, German and Spanish, every noun belongs to a group called a gender, such as masculine or feminine. This group changes small words like «the» and «a». «Le» and «la» both mean «the», and the gender of the noun decides which one you use.
explain: Grammatical gender often has nothing to do with real boys and girls. «Une table» is feminine in French, but a table is not a girl. Check the context: if the sentence is about people, gender probably means who they are; if it is about nouns in a language lesson, it means the grammar group.
fact: Gender means being a boy or a girl, a man or a woman, and the roles and ideas societies link with them.
fact: Grammatical gender is the group a noun belongs to in languages like French, German and Spanish, such as masculine or feminine.
fact: «Le» and «la» both mean «the» in French, and the noun's gender decides which one you use.
fact: «Gender stereotypes» are fixed ideas that some jobs or hobbies belong to only one gender; any gender can like football, dancing, science or cooking.
fact: «Un chapeau» (a hat) and «un manteau» (a coat) are masculine words ending in -eau, while «une casquette» (a cap) is feminine and ends in -ette.
exercise: In «un chapeau» (a hat), what is the gender of the word? | Plural | Neither, because it is a thing | Feminine | *Masculine
exercise: «Ma chambre» is said by a boy and by a girl. Why? | Because chambre means boy | Because boys say ma and girls say mon | Because it is plural | *Because chambre is a feminine word, whoever is speaking
exercise: What does «gender stereotypes» mean? | A list of boys' and girls' names | Lessons about cooking only | Rules about which school you must go to | *Fixed ideas that some jobs or hobbies belong to only one gender
test: In French, «un livre» is a book, but «une livre» means what? | A tower | *A pound | A book | A trip
test: Which word means a tower? | un livre | *une tour | une livre | un tour
exam: What does «une pomme verte et une pomme rouge» show about gender? | Gender depends on the colour of the thing | Only girls can say pomme | *A noun keeps its gender every time it is used | Apple changes gender when the colour changes
